Kathy knew that wasn\'92t true, not in her experience. She forgave Hayley for the observation; she was still TRAMPS after all. But it did make her curious. Kathy looked closer at the Elvines around Chanta. She looked at the Elvisettes down there too, though they piqued her curiosity less. She looked back at Maile and her friends.\
Hayley exhaled long and slow. \'93You noticed it too.\'94\
Kathy said nothing. Then: \'93Noticed what?\'94\
Kathy nodded: Hayley had noticed.\
\'93You been holding back,\'94 Hayley said.\
A tear formed at the corner of Kathy\'92s eye. \'93I\'92ve learned to mistrust police.\'94\
\'93So do I.\'94 Hayley turned and embraced Kathy, and gently accepted her tear with her finger tip. \'93So far, I haven\'92t arrested you for anything. And, so far, you haven\'92t turned me in for my crimes against stasis tech.\'94\
\'93That was my fault, I got you all worked up about it.\'94\
Hayley drew Kathy close. \'93You got worked up. I saw a mystery I\'92d never considered before. Now, spill.\'94\
\'93Yes, \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Detective Superintendent.\'94 Kathy drew a breath. \'93Maile was fifteen when her boyfriend\'92s car caught fire.\'94\
\'93You want me to arrest him for statutory rape?\'94\
Kathy smiled. Hayley was messing with her. She kinda liked when Hayley was messing with her.\
\'93The car fire was twenty-five years ago. Maile is forty.\'94\
Hayley nodded. \'93You\'92re so sexy when you do arithmetic.\'94\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
Kathy did not laugh. \'93Does she look like a forty-year-old woman?\'94\
\'93I\'92d guess mid-to-late twenties. Thirties, maybe.\'94 That was the detective talking.\
Kathy considered. \'93When you factor in diet, a forty-year-old Elvi will have aged another five or so years.\'94\
Hayley did the easy arithmetic in her head. \'93Those women Chanta is with\'85 do you suppose they are older than they look too?.\'94\
\'93Well, I\'92ve never seen anything like it,\'94 Kathy said. \'93Tell me, how old do you suppose Chanta is?\'94\
Hayley was recognising the pattern in her answers even as she said, \'93mid-to-late twenties.\'94\
\'93It\'92s been quite a while since I gave Chanta a birthday card with a 2 on the front.\'94\
Kathy broke from Hayley\'92s arm around her and went back to Maile\'92s group. Hayley followed.\
\'93Excuse me, Maile. May ask you a question?\'94\
\'93Of course, Aunt Kathy. Anything.\'94\
\'93Do you know Cha\'97\'85 do you know the Great Teacher.\'94\
Maile giggled. \'93Yes, we met one time.\'94\
\'93Could you tell us about it?\'94 Hayley asked.\
Kathy frowned. She almost expecting Hayley to get a notebook out.\
But Maile seemed happy to talk. It was not longer after The Holy Momma was kidnapped from the mansion the government blew up.\'94\
\'93It was the Shaktis\'97the arms dealer and her TV personality son. They took her away and only lets her out for important public occasions.\'94\
\'93The Shaktis kept her captive on their platform all the way through the Rock Against Revival,\'94 Maile\'92s friend said.\
Hayley held Kathy back from replying to that. \'93Have you ever slept with The Great Teacher?\'94 Hayley asked.\
Maile giggled again. \'93Oh, yes. We spent a weekend together at his recording studio in the ghetto. He said I was inspiring him, helping him with his writer\'92s block. He didn\'92t write anything tat weekend now \'85 Religious Minds, huh? It\'92s the most streamed song all over the country.\'94\
Maile\'92s friend vigorously pushed her in the shoulder. \'93You keep promising me you would introduce me to him! Look at her, Holy Aunties. Do we look the same age?\'94\
In the time it took Kathy and Hayley to fumble around not answering, Maile\'92s friend. \'93You see it! It\'92s unfair. I want the Great Teacher to bless me too.\'94\
Both Kathy and Hayley shut their eyes and tried to erase their visions of the blessings of the Great Teacher. Hayley recovered first. Can I have a show of hands: who was present on Bent Street Plaza at the end, when Elvi were stricken down?\'94\
Hayley surveyed Maile\'92s group of friends. Everyone with their hands up had an obvious thing in common.\
\'93Yep,\'94 Hayley said. \'93Mid-to-late twenties.\'94 \
